-- title:
--   Diagonal classes with non-norm ratio admit no twisted norm
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a finite Galois extension of $K$, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$, so that the Galois group is cyclic generated by $\sigma$; assume moreover that $[L:K] = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$ is a prime number. Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ have vanishing off-diagonal entries, $\gamma_{10} = 0$ and $\gamma_{01} = 0$, and suppose that the ratio $\gamma_{00}/\gamma_{11}$ of its diagonal entries does not lie in the image of the norm map $\mathrm{Algebra.norm}_K \colon L \to K$. Let $z$ be a unit of the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_K$ of $K$. The assertion is that there is no $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ for which the element $\mathrm{AutomorphicForm.centralScalar}\,z \cdot \mathrm{AutomorphicForm.globalPoints}\,\gamma$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ — the product of the scalar matrix with entry $z$ and of the image of $\gamma$ under the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(K) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ induced by $K \to \mathbb{A}_K$ — satisfies [`AutomorphicForm.IsNormOf`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L217) with respect to $\delta$, that is, for which there exists $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ with the image of that element under [`AutomorphicForm.toTensorGL`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L71) equal to $y^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{normString}_{K,L,\mathbb{A}_K,\sigma}(\delta) \cdot y$.
--
--   This is the class-field-theoretic input to the comparison of orbital integrals in cyclic prime-degree base change: a split diagonal class over $K$ can only be a twisted norm class adelically if the ratio of its eigenvalues is an idelic norm, hence by Hasse's norm theorem a global norm. It is used in the slope-comparison step [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_hyperbolicSlope_eq_mul_sum_slotFamilyCoeff_mul_hyperbolicSlope_of_eq_affine`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_hyperbolicSlope_eq_mul_sum_slotFamilyCoeff_mul_hyperbolicSlope_of_eq_affine), where it guarantees that non-norm classes contribute nothing.
-- source:
